1	// The typed client for the api Worker (backend-data.md §6) — the ONE module
2	// features go through to talk to the backend over http. Every URL derives
3	// from apiOrigin.ts, every request sends the session cookie (`credentials:
4	// "include"` — the cookie is SameSite=None and the api is cross-origin), and
5	// every non-2xx becomes a typed ApiError so features can branch on `.status`.
6	//
7	// TYPES-ONLY by design: this module imports nothing but types from
8	// @luminous/schema — no zod, no runtime schema values — so the web bundle
9	// stays zod-free (the same constraint that split zod off the online chunk in
10	// M8). The api already boundary-parses everything it serves; the client
