11	// The card-detail modal answers TWO questions in one surface — "which card is
12	// this?" (the seed BuilderCard the grid already holds) and "what does it do?"
13	// (the full Card, fetched on open) — and it must never let the second question
14	// blank out the first. So the header name comes straight from the seed and
15	// shows the instant the dialog opens, while the body swaps loading → ready as
16	// getCard resolves. The fetch is GUARDED against staleness: reopening on a
17	// different card (or closing) re-runs the effect, and a `cancelled` flag makes
18	// the previous in-flight promise a no-op so a slow response can't overwrite a
19	// newer one. The seed is retained through the close (the parent keeps `card`
20	// set), so the content doesn't flash empty on the way out.
